.TH qsh-trust-add-ca 1  "add-ca 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-trust\-add\-ca \- Register a foreign CA root supplied as a certificate file (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0013). Append\-only: an existing name under a different certificate is refused rather than overwritten
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh trust add\-ca\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-cert\-file\fR> <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a foreign CA root supplied as a certificate file (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0013). Append\-only: an existing name under a different certificate is refused rather than overwritten
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-file\fR \fI<PEM|\->\fR
Path to a PEM file holding exactly one `CERTIFICATE` block, or `\-` to read it from standard input
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Local name for the CA root
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
